{
  "//": [
    "The registry lockfile: exactly which extensions this store serves, and from which commit.",
    "",
    "Each entry pins a repo to one immutable commit sha. `pnpm --filter @azphalt/storefront build-catalog`",
    "fetches that commit, packs it into a .azp, signs it, and writes the bytes to registry/packages/ —",
    "which are committed. The deployment serves those bytes and nothing else.",
    "",
    "So changing what the store serves REQUIRES a reviewed commit here. There is no runtime write path,",
    "no database to drift, and no way to slip a package in without it appearing in a diff.",
    "",
    "`integrity` is the sha256 of the UNSIGNED .azp (a signature is a detached addition, so it does not",
    "perturb this). build-catalog fails on mismatch; pass --update to re-pin deliberately."
  ],
